hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3003","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Rib'iyy, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani, who informed us Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to 'Ata': \I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'You were only commanded to perform Tawaf"","" and you were not commanded to enter it.'\""\n\nHe said: \""There was no prohibition against entering it"","" but I heard him say: 'Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he entered the House"","" he supplicated in all its corners.'\""\n\nI said: \""Its corners—its four corners?\""\n\nHe said: \""Rather"","" in every direction of the House.\""\n\n---"""""
